<</CreationDate(D:20101030184415+01'00')/Subject(A non-interfering power supply device includes a free-running blocking oscillator \(10\) power supply subsystem and a circuit arrangement \(12\) that synchronizes the blocking oscillator power supply subsystem to operate at the horizontal operating freque\
ncy of a display subsystem. Synchronizing signals representative of the horizontal operating frequency of the display subsystem are generated and are used to activate the circuit arrangement that causes the blocking oscillator \(10\) to change its mode of\
 operation from free-running to a fully reset fixed frequency flyback converter. When activated, a switch \(18\) in the circuit arrangement \(12\) extends the off-time of a switching transistor \(Q1\) in the blocking oscillator \(10\). As a result, the la\
tter is forced to run at an operating frequency lower than its free-running frequency.)/PDFVersion(1.4)/Creator(Jouve S.A., TaggedPDF v1.27)/Keywords("EP291742"; "EP 291742"; "H02M 03/335"; "Power supply device with a blocking oscillator")/Producer(Adobe PDF Library 8.0)/ModDate(D:20101210193954+01'00')/Title(Power supply device with a blocking oscillator - European Patent Office - EP 291742 A3)>>
endobj
